Done. I turned it into a full 19-page working whitepaper / standardization proposal.

The paper formalizes Meaning Banks, Meaning Deposits, Meaning Reserves, Semantic Deltas, ExchangeRoutes / Trans-dict-ion, Meaning Packets, Meaning Receipts, CoSequences, the Reality Key RK-12, and a minimal interoperability standard: MBIP v0.1.

It also grounds the design against existing semantic/provenance infrastructure rather than reinventing it: ISO 704 for terminology discipline, SKOS for concept organization and mapping, PROV-O for provenance, JSON-LD for interchange, and NIST’s AI RMF as a governance context.  Pantheon integration is mapped directly to the repo’s existing Semantic Logistics, uncertainty/provenance, StateVector, ThoughtObjects, and Consequence Interface architecture. 

The important new standardization pieces are:

* RK-12 Reality Key — a portable semantic audit covering surface, referent, context, provenance, epistemic status, alternatives, relations, deltas, exchange loss, co-sequences, round-trip fidelity, and governance.
* MBIP v0.1 — a minimal data/interchange contract so implementations can differ while preserving the same semantic skeleton.
* CoSequence — your consequence → “co-sequence” operator, explicitly framed as an engineered mnemonic rather than false etymology: consequences become continuing causal sequences through other people and systems.
* Semantic sovereignty guardrails — the bank preserves competing meanings; it does not appoint itself the owner of meaning.
* Meaning Receipts — after consequential AI decisions, the system can expose which sense it used, why, what alternatives existed, and what happened downstream.
* Reality-keyed loop:
    MEANING → ACTION → WORLD → CO-SEQUENCES → DELTA → MEANING′

